{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\nimpl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D> {\n    /// Borrow the inspection context shared by this criterion's operations.\n    pub fn inspection(&self) -> &InspectionContext<'d, D>;\n}\n```\n\n`ValidationContext::inspection()` exposes the execution's `InspectionContext`.\nThe ask builder passes that context to `Agent::run`. The supplied `ToolAgent`\nimplements graph-node reads, outgoing-edge queries, and delivery recording by\ndelegating to that same context's operations.\n\nBorrowing the context does not record an input. The reads and edge selections\nperformed through it contribute the observations described below.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The structural obligations are met.\n\n- **Accessor signature.** `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#1/fn[inspection]` has the required signature. It is `pub fn inspection(&self) -> &InspectionContext<'d, D>` in `impl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D>`. It only returns `&self.inspection`, so it borrows the execution's context and records no input.\n- **Ask builder passes the context.** `procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]` calls `agent.run(request, &self.ctx.inspection)`. The `Agent::run` signature in `procedure.rs#trait[Agent]/fn[run]` takes `inspection: &'a InspectionContext<'_, D>`. The ask builder therefore passes the same context to the agent.\n- **`ToolAgent` takes and keeps that context.** `agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` receives `inspection` and stores the reference in `GraphSession`, defined at `agent/tools.rs#struct[GraphSession]`.\n- **`ToolAgent` delegates to the context's operations.**\n  - Node reads: `agent/tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[dispatch]` handles `read_node` with `inspection.prepare_read` and `graph().format_node_content`.\n  - Outgoing-edge queries: the same function handles `outgoing_edges` with `inspection.prepare_edges`.\n  - Delivery recording: `agent/tools.rs#impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[delivered]` records pending observations with `inspection.observe_read` and `inspection.observe_edges`.\n\nThe text names no refining declaration that would need separate assessment. No {fixme} acknowledgments are present, and I found no structural gap.",
